I fell in love with film when I was a  when I was 13 years old and I wanted to  become a director I grew up in  Switzerland and people felt that it was  like becoming an astronaut and going to  the moon but I pursued that dream I went  to film school actually that was a major  thing for me to be accepted at UCLA it  was one of the premiere film schools in  America and I went there I planned to be  there for four years and get a BA  however that was not enough so I decided  to go to graduate school and the idea  was to have made some films and be a  director however when I came back to  Switzerland there wasn't really any any  work in film so I decided to go back to  the United States extend my education  but not to pursue directing but editing  which was something I fell in love with  while I was doing my my films at a film  school I really discovered the power of  editing while doing documentaries and  short films  I think if if you want to become an  editor at least you've experienced some  form of passion for film I think that's  key to have that passion because you're  gonna be working many hours but besides  that you have to have an imaginative  mind you like to do things with your  hands and trying to solve problems you  have to use your imagination so if you  have all those qualities then you should  become an editor or at least pursue that  interest but I think the key to all that  is simply have a love and passion for it  when I was starting  an assistant the best at what advice I  got was from very early on from Claire  Simpson who was editing Wall Street at  the time and she also had worked with  one of the great editors she was  assisting Dede Allen so she told me the  story that the island told her she's  kind of like the godmother of editors  cut Bonnie and Clyde and you know a lot  of other great pictures because the the  mother of modern and she heard what  Beebe Island told Claire Simpson and  Claire Simpson told me is like  everything is about rhythm and that  stayed with me as a very good advice it  is rhythm it moves you it it also  reflects the rhythm of your heart in  terms of emotion so rhythm is very  important and the other advice that I  think about is what Oliver said they  said that we no matter what you do don't  be boring so that's about it
 

